{
  "dom_id": "step-q225057",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6.5)$ given below, compute $P(3\\le X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0430\\,$ | $\\,0.1118\\,$ | $\\,0.2237\\,$ | $\\,0.3690\\,$ | $\\,0.5265\\,$ | $\\,0.6728\\,$ | $\\,0.7916\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6728-0.0430 \\\\  & =0.6298.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
